Packaging filsys for Distributions
==================================

This file is for distribution packagers who want to add filsys to their
distro's package repository.  Template packaging files for several systems
are provided under `packaging/`.  Each is roughly 90% complete — the packager
fills in maintainer details, changelog, and distro-specific adjustments.

What filsys Is
--------------

filsys is a FUSE driver and set of disk utilities for Research Unix (the
PDP-7 through V7, 32V, and Coherent) filesystem images on a modern host.  It
ships four tools: `mount.filsys` (the FUSE mount), `findfs.filsys` (locate
filesystem superblocks/partitions on a raw disk image), `mkfs.filsys` (create
a filesystem), and `fsck.filsys` (check one).

Dependencies
------------

Build-time:
  - a C17 compiler (gcc or clang)
  - libfuse3 development headers, found via pkg-config (`fuse3.pc`):
    Debian/Ubuntu `libfuse3-dev`, Fedora `fuse3-devel`, Arch/Alpine `fuse3`
  - GNU make; autoconf/automake only to regenerate `configure` (which is
    shipped)

Runtime:
  - libfuse3 (`libfuse3.so.3`)

How the Build Works
-------------------

    ./configure && make && make check && make install

Install layout (default prefix `/usr/local`):

    $(bindir)/mount.filsys     the FUSE mount driver
    $(bindir)/findfs.filsys    the superblock/partition finder
    $(bindir)/mkfs.filsys      create a V7 filesystem
    $(bindir)/fsck.filsys      check a V7 filesystem
    $(mandir)/man5/filsys.5    the filesystem-format manual
    $(mandir)/man1/{mount,findfs,mkfs,fsck}.filsys.1

License
-------

filsys is dual-licensed, by file origin (see COPYING): the driver source is
ISC, and the V7/32V filesystem-format code is under the Caldera "Ancient
UNIX" license.  Record this as "ISC AND Caldera" in license metadata.

Per-Distribution Notes
======================

RPM (Fedora / RHEL / CentOS)
----------------------------

  Files:  packaging/filsys.spec

  Customize: URL/Source0, the %changelog entry.
  Build:  rpmbuild -ba packaging/filsys.spec
  Submit: Fedora Package Review process / EPEL.

Debian / Ubuntu
---------------

  Files:  packaging/debian/

  Customize: debian/changelog, debian/control Maintainer, debian/copyright.
  Build:  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc
  Submit: File an ITP against wnpp.

Arch Linux
----------

  Files:  packaging/PKGBUILD

  Customize: Maintainer line, sha256sums (updpkgsums).
  Build:  makepkg -si
  Submit: AUR.

Alpine Linux
------------

  Files:  packaging/alpine/APKBUILD

  Customize: Maintainer line, sha512sums (abuild checksum).
  Build:  abuild -r
  Submit: MR against aports.git.

FreeBSD
-------

  Files:  packaging/freebsd/

  Customize: MAINTAINER email, distinfo (real SHA256/SIZE).
  Build:  make -C packaging/freebsd install (in a ports tree)
  Submit: FreeBSD bug / send-pr, category "ports".

OpenBSD
-------

  Files:  packaging/openbsd/

  Customize: MAINTAINER email, pkg/PLIST after a test install.
  Build:  make -C packaging/openbsd install (in a ports tree)
  Submit: diff to ports@openbsd.org.

NetBSD
------

  Files:  packaging/netbsd/

  Customize: MAINTAINER email, distinfo (make distinfo).
  Build:  bmake install (in a pkgsrc tree)
  Submit: diff to pkgsrc-wip / pkgsrc-changes.

Gentoo
------

  Files:  packaging/gentoo/

  Customize: metadata.xml maintainer, ebuild SRC_URI, KEYWORDS.
  Build:  ebuild packaging/gentoo/filsys-1.0.0.ebuild manifest && emerge
  Submit: bug at bugs.gentoo.org (category "Ebuild") or the GURU overlay.

NixOS
-----

  Files:  packaging/nixos/default.nix

  Customize: fetchFromGitHub owner/hash, meta.maintainers.
  Build:  nix-build -E 'with import <nixpkgs> {}; callPackage ./packaging/nixos/default.nix {}'
  Submit: PR against nixpkgs.

Slackware
---------

  Files:  packaging/slackware/

  Customize: filsys.SlackBuild copyright, filsys.info MD5SUM/MAINTAINER, slack-desc URL.
  Build:  source filsys.info && sh filsys.SlackBuild
  Submit: SlackBuilds.org (SBo).
